course: dictionary
lesson: 7378
title: Plough: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have several meanings. Plough can be a farm tool, a verb for turning over soil, or the name of a group of stars. Read the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: «Water buffaloes pulled ploughs through wet rice fields.» Here a plough is a big tool, because buffaloes pull it and it goes through the fields. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: «The car ploughed into the fence.» Here plough is a verb meaning to move forward with force. «Plough through homework» means keep going with something hard or boring. The words around the word tell you which meaning is right.
fact: Plough as a noun means a big farm tool that turns over and breaks up soil so it is ready for planting.
fact: Plough as a verb means to turn over soil, or to move forward with force, as in «the car ploughed into the fence».
fact: «Plough through» means to keep going with something hard or boring, such as «plough through homework».
fact: A snowplough is a machine that clears snow from roads.
fact: The Plough is a group of seven bright stars, the UK name for the Big Dipper, and its two Pointers lead to the Pole Star.
exercise: «The farmer used a plough to break up the soil before planting.» What is a plough? | A kind of snow | *A big farm tool, pulled by a tractor or animals | A type of boat | A bright star in the night sky
exercise: «The car ploughed into the fence.» What does ploughed mean here? | *Moved forward with force and hit the fence | Kept going with homework | Turned over soil in a field | Shone brightly in the dark
exercise: Sam says «plough through homework» means to finish it quickly. What does plough through mean? | Lose it under the sofa | Turn it over with a tool | *Keep going with something hard or boring | Eat it up very fast
test: «Gulls follow a tractor ploughing a field, because ploughing turns up worms and grubs.» In this sentence, ploughing is a verb meaning what? | To count bright stars | To clear snow from a road | To shine brightly | *To turn over soil with a tool
test: Which name is used in the UK for seven bright stars, the one that points to the Pole Star? | The Milky Way | The Snowplough | *The Plough | The Southern Cross
exam: Which meaning of plough fits «Water buffaloes pulled ploughs through wet rice fields»? | *A big farm tool pulled by animals | To move forward with force | To clear snow from roads | A group of seven stars
